completed_at: "2026-08-27T05:04:09.719Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 180
acceptance_criteria: "Mixed-case and lowercase Beads IDs round-trip without spelling changes; all dependency, parent, comment, and history references resolve to the preserved IDs; collision detection remains fail-closed across case-sensitive and case-insensitive filesystems; Windows, Linux, package, and installed-consumer tests pass"
goal: project management = context management
objective: Preserve canonical external identity across migrations
value: "Keeps cross-system references, relationships, and audit trails stable"
why_now: GitHub issue #860 reports an active identity-corruption defect in migration
parent: pm-ugqx
risk: high
confidence: 95
resolution: Implemented
expected_result: "Preserved Beads source IDs retain exact spelling across item files, parents, dependencies, history, lookup, and collision checks."
actual_result: "Mixed-case IDs and relationships now round-trip exactly, hash shorthand resolves exact case, and case-insensitive duplicate/collision preflight fails before any importer write."
